  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For a hotel in Mexico that needs **strong lifestyle positioning**, the best brands to consider are **Kimpton, Hotel Indigo, Canopy by Hilton, Motto by Hilton, Live Aqua, Grupo Habita, Habitas, Design Hotels, Preferred Hotels & Resorts’ Lifestyle/L.V.X. collections, and Lifestylehotels™**.[1][2][3][4][7][8][9][10][13][14]\n\n- **Kimpton**: IHG is explicitly growing its **Luxury & Lifestyle** portfolio in Mexico, with existing and forthcoming projects including **Kimpton Mas Olas Todos Santos** and **Kimpton Tres Rios**.[10]\n- **Hotel Indigo**: Also part of IHG’s **Luxury & Lifestyle** set, with **Hotel Indigo Playa del Carmen** already opened in Mexico, making it a clear lifestyle-oriented flag for urban or resort-adjacent markets.[10]\n- **Canopy by Hilton**: Hilton introduced **Canopy by Hilton Cancun La Isla** as its upscale lifestyle brand’s debut in the Caribbean and Latin America, signaling fit for a locally rooted, boutique-style positioning.[1]\n- **Motto by Hilton**: Hilton describes Motto as an **urban lifestyle brand** centered on local immersion, and it launched in Mexico with **Motto by Hilton Tulum**.[9]\n- **Live Aqua**: Posadas says **Live Aqua** is its first lifestyle brand, built around multi-sensory experiences and design-led luxury; it already has a strong Mexico footprint.[8][13][16]\n- **Grupo Habita**: This is one of Mexico’s most credible homegrown lifestyle operators, described as a pioneering lifestyle hotel brand with multiple properties across Mexico.[2][12]\n- **Habitas**: Strong for experience-led, design-forward, sustainability-minded concepts; it is frequently positioned among Mexico’s standout boutique/lifestyle options.[18][11]\n- **Design Hotels**: Best if the owner wants a curated, design-centric affiliation rather than a conventional branded full-service flag; Mexico has a broad selection of member hotels.[4][17]\n- **Preferred Hotels & Resorts – Lifestyle / L.V.X.**: Useful if the owner wants soft-brand independence with lifestyle credibility; in Mexico, member hotels are already aligned to these collections.[7][13][15]\n- **Lifestylehotels™**: A fit for highly individual, authentic, locally grounded hotels; its Mexico entry specifically emphasizes contemporary design, local influence, sustainability, and relaxed luxury.[3][14]\n\nIf the owner wants the **most “flag-like” branded options with lifestyle equity**, the strongest shortlist is usually **Kimpton, Hotel Indigo, Canopy, Motto, and Live Aqua**.[1][8][9][10] If the goal is a more **independent, design-led, culturally distinct positioning**, **Grupo Habita, Habitas, Design Hotels, Preferred Hotels & Resorts, and Lifestylehotels™** are better fits.[2][3][4][7][11][14]\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a **Mexico-specific shortlist by city/asset type** such as **beach resort, urban lifestyle, mixed-use, or upper-upscale conversion**.",
